{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The Servlet API exposes the full request path as "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "requestURI"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and further sub-divides it into "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "contextPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pathInfo"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " whose values vary depending on how a Servlet is mapped. From these inputs, Spring MVC needs to determine the lookup path to use for mapping handlers, which should exclude the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "contextPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and any "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletMapping"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " prefix, if applicable."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pathInfo"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " are decoded and that makes them impossible to compare directly to the full "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "requestURI"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " in order to derive the lookupPath and that makes it necessary to decode the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "requestURI"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". However this introduces its own issues because the path may contain encoded reserved characters such as "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "\"/\""
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "\";\""
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that can in turn alter the structure of the path after they are decoded which can also lead to security issues. In addition, Servlet containers may normalize the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to varying degrees which makes it further impossible to perform "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "startsWith"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " comparisons against the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "requestURI"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This is why it is best to avoid reliance on the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " which comes with the prefix-based "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " mapping type. If the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DispatcherServlet"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is mapped as the default Servlet with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "\"/\""
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or otherwise without a prefix with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "\"/*\""
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and the Servlet container is 4.0+ then Spring MVC is able to detect the Servlet mapping type and avoid use of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pathInfo"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " altogether. On a 3.1 Servlet container, assuming the same Servlet mapping types, the equivalent can be achieved by providing a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "UrlPathHelper"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "alwaysUseFullPath=true"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " via "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Path Matching"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/webmvc/mvc-config/path-matching.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " in the MVC config."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Fortunately the default Servlet mapping "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "\"/\""
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is a good choice. However, there is still an issue in that the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "requestURI"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " needs to be decoded to make it possible to compare to controller mappings. This is again undesirable because of the potential to decode reserved characters that alter the path structure. If such characters are not expected, then you can reject them (like the Spring Security HTTP firewall), or you can configure "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "UrlPathHelper"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "urlDecode=false"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " but controller mappings will need to match to the encoded path which may not always work well. Furthermore, sometimes the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DispatcherServlet"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " needs to share the URL space with another Servlet and may need to be mapped by prefix."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The above issues are addressed when using "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "PathPatternParser"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and parsed patterns, as an alternative to String path matching with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AntPathMatcher"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "PathPatternParser"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " has been available for use in Spring MVC from version 5.3, and is enabled by default from version 6.0. Unlike "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AntPathMatcher"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " which needs either the lookup path decoded or the controller mapping encoded, a parsed "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "PathPattern"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " matches to a parsed representation of the path called "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "RequestPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", one path segment at a time. This allows decoding and sanitizing path segment values individually without the risk of altering the structure of the path. Parsed "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "PathPattern"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " also supports the use of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "servletPath"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " prefix mapping as long as a Servlet path mapping is used and the prefix is kept simple, i.e. it has no encoded characters. For pattern syntax details and comparison, see "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Pattern Comparison"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/webmvc/mvc-controller/ann-requestmapping.html#mvc-ann-requestmapping-pattern-comparison"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Path Matching"
      }
    ]
  }
}
